      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2024/07/adidas-adizero-sl-2-review-2024.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Full-length Lightstrike Pro wrapped by Lightstrike 2.0 creates a well-cushioned ride that is mildly to moderately soft with good impact protection; heel transitions are smooth, but the 10 mm drop makes the heel feel higher.",
        "Responsiveness: The midsole delivers noticeable bounce and resilient energy return, with faster turnover and smoother toe-off at tempo/uptempo paces; it is responsive for workouts but not the snappiest for all-out track work.",
        "Stability: The shoe remains neutral with slight overall flexibility (not highly torsionally rigid), a fairly flexible heel counter, mild central guidance from the foam setup, and subtle forefoot flaring/lateral support to keep it from feeling unstable.",
        "Durability: Outsole durability is excellent, with extensive rubber and no reported wear after ~40 miles; traction is strong on roads, indicating above-average material longevity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2024/06/adidas-adizero-sl2-video-review-light.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The shoe is described as soft, with a 36 mm heel and 26-27 mm forefoot stack suggesting solid daily impact protection and a cushioned heel/forefoot feel.",
        "Responsiveness: It is described as energetic, likely helped by the full-length Lightstrike Pro insert, and feels versatile at most paces but not ideal for very fast efforts.",
        "Stability: The provided text does not include specific observations on torsional rigidity, heel counter stiffness, or lateral support.",
        "Durability: The provided text does not provide findings on outsole wear or long-term material longevity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/adidas-adizero-sl-2-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The Lightstrike Pro + Lightstrike 2.0 setup is softer without feeling dead, absorbs impact well, and gives notably strong forefoot protection with a smooth heel/forefoot transition.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is consistently described as smooth and snappy, with solid rebound, bounce, and energy return that can handle both easy miles and faster tempo pace changes.",
        "Stability: Heel lockdown is secure (snug upper/heel pillows), and the foam mix adds some control, but overall stability support is low for pronators and lateral support is limited for runners needing true stability.",
        "Durability: Despite no Continental rubber, outsole traction/coverage is rated very good, and the mono-mesh upper is described as durable and abrasion-resistant, indicating good material longevity."
      ]
    }
